# The lab's phone-to-phone peer, registered at the lab's own Kamailio
# (interop/kamailio/kamailio.cfg) as three accounts sharing one password --
# the same shape Asterisk's own SRTP and DTLS-SRTP endpoints already take in
# this lab (interop/asterisk/pjsip.conf), and for the same reason: a media
# policy is set once per account, so a call each flow places is a call this
# file's own capture can tell apart from the others without reading the SDP.
#
# answermode=auto: this stack places every call against this peer, so
# nothing here ever dials out, and answermode is the account parameter
# module_app menu.so reads to answer one on its own. answerdelay=0 so a
# flow's own patience is spent waiting on the far end's real work, not on a
# delay this file chose. audio_codecs=pcmu,pcma names the same two laws
# every other server in this lab offers, in the order the harness's own
# catalogue offers them (docs/11-testing.md). dtmfmode=rtpevent is RFC
# 4733's named telephone event; baresip's other choice is SIP INFO, which
# this peer is not asked to speak.
#
<sip:baresip@kamailio>;auth_pass=baresippass;answermode=auto;answerdelay=0;audio_codecs=pcmu,pcma;dtmfmode=rtpevent

# SDES (RFC 4568), required rather than offered: srtp-mand answers RTP/SAVP
# alone and refuses a call that cannot be keyed by it, which is what this
# lab's own SRTP flow asks of every peer it runs against.
<sip:baresip-srtp@kamailio>;auth_pass=baresippass;answermode=auto;answerdelay=0;audio_codecs=pcmu,pcma;dtmfmode=rtpevent;mediaenc=srtp-mand

# DTLS-SRTP (RFC 5764). modules/dtls_srtp self-signs its own certificate at
# startup and trusts whatever fingerprint the far end's SDP carries, the
# same fingerprint-only check RFC 8122 section 5 and RFC 5763 section 5 ask
# for and the same shape Asterisk's dtls_auto_generate_cert=yes takes in
# this lab. rtcp_mux=yes: this stack's own DTLS association runs on the one
# port its RTP and RTCP already share (RFC 5764 section 4.2) and refuses a
# call the far end will not multiplex on it, and rtcp_mux is off unless an
# account asks for it (src/config.c's own default).
<sip:baresip-dtls@kamailio>;auth_pass=baresippass;answermode=auto;answerdelay=0;audio_codecs=pcmu,pcma;dtmfmode=rtpevent;mediaenc=dtls_srtp;rtcp_mux=yes
